                <pb facs="0518" n="423" xml:id="pg423"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13767: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-15T16:00:00+08:00">December 15, 1936—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 15—9:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>352. Your 79, December 14, 1 p.m. I expect to see Minister for Foreign Affairs at
                    4 p.m. today and convey Department’s message. Nanking quiet. Situation
                    unchanged. Government anxiously awaiting news of Donald’s visit Sian. Troops
                    continue to move north.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
